        "thought_text": "The current approach of using a prefix sum array and inserting a 1 when a zero-sum subsegment is detected is not sufficient. It fails to handle cases where multiple zero-sum subsegments overlap or when inserting a single element doesn't resolve all zero-sum subsegments. A more robust approach would be to use a stack-based approach to track prefix sums and detect zero-sum subsegments, while also keeping track of the frequency of each prefix sum to determine the minimum number of insertions needed to break all zero-sum subsegments.",
